HOW TO DEPLOY TO STAGING
------------------------

# Explicit file list -- do NOT go back to `sudo cp ~/dokimion/config/staging/s-dokimion/* .`
# or a `*.h` wildcard. This directory also holds s-dokimion-staging.key (the web-server SAN
# cert's PRIVATE key); a wildcard copy would drop it into sites-available -- the staging twin
# of security_hardening_production.md finding H2 (needless world-readable private key on the
# load balancer). The LB never presents that key; it only needs the public .crt to verify
# upstreams (proxy_pass.h).

# load_balancer.conf is stored ONCE in the repo, under production/dokimion, and is shared by
# the production and staging load balancers. The seven .h files are this LB's own (staging
# upstreams + staging certs); every include in load_balancer.conf resolves against
# sites-available, so they all land there.
CONF=~/dokimion/config/production/dokimion     # shared LB config
H=~/dokimion/config/staging/s-dokimion         # this LB's host/env includes
sudo install -m 644 -t /etc/nginx/sites-available \
  $CONF/load_balancer.conf \
  $H/servers.h $H/certificates.h $H/server_name.h \
  $H/rate_limiting.h $H/proxy_pass.h $H/http_return.h $H/lb_client_cert.h

sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx

# security_hardening H1 — load_balancer.conf includes lb_client_cert.h (installed above);
# nginx refuses to start if it is missing. It ships inert (the two proxy_ssl_certificate
# directives are commented) until the LB client cert is issued and enabled -- see
# mtls_h1_deploy.md, Phase 4.

# Certificates are deliberately NOT part of this sync -- they are already installed on the box.
# If rebuilding the LB from scratch, install:
#   - s-dokimion-staging.crt (mode 644) -- web-server SAN cert, used by
#     proxy_ssl_trusted_certificate to verify the s-dokimion1/2/3 upstreams (proxy_pass.h)
#   - test_staging.languagetechnology.org.pem/.key -- client-facing cert (certificates.h)
# Do NOT put s-dokimion-staging.key on the LB at all; the LB never presents it.
